# zl1 heat-fix chain -- the end-state reader, fixed and read on the device
# host date: 2026-09-25T17:53:30Z   (device clock is wrong and is not used)
# device: root@10.15.19.82 (serial 33e80afe), USB 18d1:d001 (RNDIS), boot_id 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5
#         (the boot the one-boot runbook ran on; read again at the end of this stage, no reboot since)

## 1. the FIXED reader, the shipped command, read-only:
$ scripts/host/zl1-heat-fix-chain.sh --status
zl1 heat-fix chain -- status (read-only)
  device:  root@10.15.19.82 (serial 33e80afe)
  boot_id: 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5

  netwatch: file=present fn=has-ensure_addrs unit=active
  keeper: gone
  addrs: 192.168.2.15/24=present 10.15.19.82/24=present
  governors: interactive interactive interactive interactive

  read it as the chain: the netwatch file must carry ensure_addrs() BEFORE the keeper is retired,
  and the keeper being gone with BOTH of the device's own addresses still present is the end state
  the third step buys. (The addresses are read on the device and are the device's: the host's own
  address is a host-side fact and is not asked for here -- see the note above dev_end_state.)

